Our codec alone, measured end to end (whole test_text: 470M values, decoded layer by layer, bit-exact). For each link the mode with the shortest transfer among: fused 32x8, uniform (9.011 bits/value, 7.6 G values/s); fused 64x8, uniform (9.004 bits/value, 5.9 G values/s); fused 32x4, uniform (9.004 bits/value, 8.1 G values/s); fused 16x4, uniform (9.011 bits/value, 5.0 G values/s); fused 64x16, uniform (9.011 bits/value, 4.2 G values/s); fused 32x4, exact (8.945 bits/value, 4.7 G values/s); per layer, dense product, uniform (9.025 bits/value, 15.1 G values/s); per layer, dense product, exact (8.965 bits/value, 10.8 G values/s); per layer, rank 512 product, uniform (9.221 bits/value, 18.5 G values/s); per layer, rank 384 product, uniform (9.296 bits/value, 19.1 G values/s); per layer, rank 256 product, uniform (9.405 bits/value, 20.5 G values/s). SplitZip: 12.021 bits/value on the same document, its measured A4500 decode speed. Ideal link as above; the bands are typical deployments (see the doc).

