## Our prediction in SplitZip's format: the real codec (kv_compare/szcodec.py)

Fixed-length codes chosen per value by our one-step prediction (sign agreement + magnitude residual, per-context b raw bits and a k-bit code, escapes carry the word), so every value of a tile is placed by two prefix sums, as in SplitZip; no entropy coder. Code books from train0, train1; measured on test_text on the NVIDIA RTX A4500, bit-exact round trip checked. Reduced rank: the second product runs inside the decoding kernel (tensor cores), so the int32 products never go through memory. Bits include the 32-bit segment starts and padding.

