## AQUA-KV's protocol: WikiText-2 perplexity with a streaming compressed cache

The authors' evaluation (goodevening13/aquakv@e744183, evaluate_perplexity.py) for every method, in one harness (kv_compare/streaming.py): the whole WikiText-2 test split in 8192-token windows (35 windows), 32 tokens per forward pass, the first 4 tokens and the most recent tokens (at least 128 before a block is compressed) in BF16, every older token compressed and read back. Perplexity with the authors' BF16 loss (comparable to the paper) and with a float32 loss from the same logits (resolves small gaps; the change is per window, mean +- standard error). Bits per value: over the compressed values (as the papers count) and for the whole cache at the end of each window. Size: one window's KV (8,192 tokens, 470M values; 896 MiB in BF16) at those rates.

